<BaseLayout
  title="Helping a consultancy decide where to focus its commercial effort."
  description="Go-to-market research helping a consultancy decide where to focus sales and marketing effort through customer profiling."
  canonicalPath="/work/go-to-market/"
  enhanceDecks
>
<main id="main">
<section class="case-hero"><a class="back-link" href={withBase('#work')}>← All work</a><p class="eyebrow">CASE 05 / RESEARCH · COMMERCIAL STRATEGY</p><h1>Helping a consultancy decide where to focus its commercial effort.</h1><p class="case-intro">A consultancy needed to decide which prospective customers to focus on for sales outreach and marketing campaigns. The research connected commercial history with stakeholder perspectives to define better-fit company profiles and buyer personas.</p><div aria-label="Case at a glance" class="quick-read"><div><span class="quick-label">Challenge</span><p>Choose which prospects deserve sales and marketing effort.</p></div><div><span class="quick-label">Contribution</span><p>Combine commercial history, interviews and market analysis.</p></div><div><span class="quick-label">Delivered</span><p>Ideal, acceptable and incompatible profiles, plus buyer personas.</p></div></div><div class="case-metadata"><div><span>CONTEXT</span><p>Consultancy · Client name withheld</p></div><div><span>MY FOCUS</span><p>CX, research, data analysis &amp; strategy</p></div><div><span>SCOPE</span><p>Customer profiling &amp; prospecting priorities</p></div><div><span>TIMEFRAME</span><p>4-week project</p></div></div></section><div class="case-cover source-cover"><button aria-label="Enlarge: Company profiles" class="image-open" data-caption="Company profiles" type="button"><img alt="Company profiles" data-source-index="13" draggable="false" loading="eager" src={withBase('assets/source-013.webp')}/><span aria-hidden="true">Expand ↗</span></button></div>
<nav aria-label="Case sections" class="case-nav"><a href="#challenge">At a glance</a><a href="#decisions">The story</a><a href="#outcomes">Outputs &amp; outcomes</a></nav>
<div class="case-content">
<section class="challenge" id="challenge"><p class="eyebrow">THE BUSINESS QUESTION</p><h2>Which prospects are the best fit for the consultancy, and what should shape outreach to them?</h2><div class="contribution"><div><h3>My contribution</h3><p>My role brought together customer experience, data analysis, research and strategy. Working with a multidisciplinary team, the project translated business information and interviews into customer profiles and buyer perspectives for commercial planning.</p></div><div><h3>Collaboration</h3><p>Innovation Strategist, CX Strategist, UX Researcher, Marketing Analyst and a trainee.</p></div></div><div class="facts"><div><strong>4</strong><span>weeks of work</span></div><div><strong>3</strong><span>company-fit profiles</span></div><div><strong>2</strong><span>research views: internal &amp; external</span></div></div></section><div id="decisions">
<section class="chapter story-stage" id="decision-1"><p class="chapter-index">01 / DECISION</p><div><h2>Connect commercial history with market context</h2><p class="decision-summary">Use historical business and market context to question future customer fit.</p><details class="decision-context"><summary>Read the decision context <span aria-hidden="true">＋</span></summary><p>The team reviewed business transaction data and market information to understand historical negotiations, service demand and potential customer segments. Interviews with internal leaders explored commercial priorities and operational constraints.</p></details><blockquote>Past customers were evidence to examine, rather than the automatic definition of future customers.</blockquote></div></section>
<figure class="story-image wide-image"><div class="artifact-heading"><p class="eyebrow">PROJECT EVIDENCE</p><h3>Company data analysis</h3></div><button aria-label="Enlarge: Company data analysis" class="image-open" data-caption="Company data analysis" type="button"><img alt="Company data analysis" data-source-index="14" draggable="false" loading="lazy" src={withBase('assets/source-014.webp')}/><span aria-hidden="true">Expand ↗</span></button><figcaption>Select the image to explore the detail.</figcaption></figure>
<figure class="story-image wide-image"><div class="artifact-heading"><p class="eyebrow">PROJECT EVIDENCE</p><h3>Desk research</h3></div><button aria-label="Enlarge: Desk research" class="image-open" data-caption="Desk research" type="button"><img alt="Desk research" data-source-index="15" draggable="false" loading="lazy" src={withBase('assets/source-015.webp')}/><span aria-hidden="true">Expand ↗</span></button><figcaption>Select the image to explore the detail.</figcaption></figure>
<section class="chapter story-stage" id="decision-2"><p class="chapter-index">02 / DECISION</p><div><h2>Understand the buyer and refine the fit</h2><p class="decision-summary">Bring company attributes and buyer needs into the same analysis.</p><details class="decision-context"><summary>Read the decision context <span aria-hidden="true">＋</span></summary><p>Client and prospect interviews explored needs and buying considerations. Gartner consultant input helped refine the analysis. The work brought company attributes together with operational, technological and behavioural considerations.</p></details><blockquote>Company fit and the people involved in buying were complementary views.</blockquote></div></section>
